{
  "valuation_insights": "## Annual and Quarterly Results for Costco Wholesale Corporation (COST)\n\n- The annual total revenue for fiscal year ended 2026-08-30 was $303.154 billion, up 10.14% from $275.235 billion in fiscal year ended 2025-08-31 [C:revenue_2026].\n- Operating income for fiscal 2026 was $11.685 billion yielding an operating margin of 3.85% [C:operating_income_2026] [C:operating_margin_2026].\n- Net income attributable to the company was $9.226 billion for fiscal 2026, increased from $8.099 billion prior year [C:net_income_2026].\n- GAAP diluted earnings per share was $20.76 in 2026 versus $18.21 in 2025 [C:diluted_eps_2026].\n- Return on average equity was 28.40%, calculated using net income over average stockholders' equity between 2025 and 2026 year ends [C:return_on_equity_2026].\n- Debt to equity ratio including current portion of long-term debt was 0.172, representing moderate leverage [C:debt_to_equity_2026].\n- Free cash flow for fiscal year 2026 was $9.382 billion, computed as net cash provided by operating activities minus capital expenditures [C:free_cash_flow_2026].\n- Latest quarter net sales increased 11.2% to $93.9 billion from $84.4 billion last year, though total revenue including membership fees was $95.723 billion this quarter [C:quarter_revenue_4Q] (not fully established for total revenue quarterly).\n- GAAP diluted EPS for the fourth quarter was $6.75, benefiting from a one-time tariff refund impact of $0.15 per diluted share [C:quarter_diluted_eps_4Q].\n- Based on the closing price of $904.70 on 2026-09-23 and annual diluted EPS of $20.76, the price-to-earnings ratio stands at approximately 43.58 [C:pe_ratio_2026].\n- Peer operating margins on a consistent total revenue basis show Walmart at 4.18%, Target at 4.88%, and BJ's Wholesale at 3.81% for their latest reported fiscal years, allowing relative margin comparison [C:peer_margins].\n\n**Caution:** The revenue figure uses the tag RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax, usually representing total revenue, but verification is advised as it might exclude certain income or be reported as net sales in some contexts.\n\nInsight: Costco's debt structure shows a significant increase in the current portion of long-term debt from $75 million in 2025 to $2.248 billion in 2026 (10-K line 81 L000081), indicating a concentration of debt maturing within one year, which may affect liquidity management and refinancing risk. This maturity concentration detail is not highlighted in the earnings release opening paragraph.\n\n---",
